{"id":"2062846778148394750","kind":"article","title":"局部最优 & 贪心选择","author":"Gwern Branwen","original_authors":["Gwern Branwen"],"original_source_urls":["https://gwern.net/note/local-optima"],"publisher":"Jarrett Ye","column":"Gwern Branwen","date":"2026-07-23","updated":"2026-07-23","votes":14,"comment_count":1,"minutes":4,"chars":1902,"keywords":["局部最优","贪心选择","风险厌恶","创造性破坏","决策研究","文献目录"],"summary":"主题目录：本页围绕局部最优、贪心选择、风险厌恶与创造性破坏，按灾难、迁移、重大决策和人类流动等主题整理研究与文章链接，并附少数研究范围注释，供读者查找相关文献。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/2062846778148394750","restoration":null,"toc":[],"html":"<p data-pid=\"VU4R2iis\">关于局部最优/贪心性/风险厌恶/创造性破坏（例如波特假说或股权溢价之谜）的一些有趣链接；相关现象有时会在灾难中显现出来。</p><blockquote data-pid=\"YAIX6biO\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"http://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>感谢主要译者 GPT-5.6-sol，校对 Jarrett Ye<br/>首次发表于 2021-03-24。状态：已完成；置信度说明：log；重要性：5/10。<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/note/local-optima\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Local Optima &amp; Greedy Choices · Gwern.net</a></blockquote><ul><li data-pid=\"iAVCxSW5\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/economics/automation/index\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《自动化犹如殖民浪潮》</a></li><li data-pid=\"kXflpA0g\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.oreilly.com/content/piracy-is-progressive-taxation-and-other-thoughts-on-the-evolution-of-online-distribution/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《默默无闻对作者和艺术创作者的威胁远甚于盗版》</a>，Timothy O'Reilly 2002</li><li data-pid=\"bIgNvXbK\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Luck-Factor-Scientific-Wiseman-Paperback/dp/B00IGYST8M/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《幸运因素》</a>，Wiseman 2004</li><li data-pid=\"550w8iAT\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/psychology/okcupid/themathematicsofbeauty.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《OKCupid：美貌的数学》</a>，Rudder 2011</li><li data-pid=\"PwKB5rGW\"><b>战争/灾难/崩溃</b>：</li><ul><li data-pid=\"Z7YpP-yF\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/economics/1995-bendavid.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《大战、大崩盘与稳态增长：关于一个旧有典型事实的一些新证据》</a>，Ben-David &amp; Papell 1995；<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/economics/2002-skidmore.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《自然灾害会促进长期增长吗？》</a>，Skidmore &amp; Toya 2002</li><li data-pid=\"exX8iieg\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/economics/2018-deryugina.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《卡特里娜飓风对受灾者的经济影响：来自个人纳税申报表的证据》</a>，Deryugina et al 2014</li><li data-pid=\"lcPeH_cc\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/economics/2018-aiyar.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《因 Sardar Sarovar 大坝项目被迫搬迁并重新安置的人，如今是否比没有搬迁的昔日邻居过得更好？》</a>，Aiyar &amp; Kaushal 2018</li><li data-pid=\"a5B7YMA7\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://eprints.lse.ac.uk/63832/1/dp1372.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《被迫尝试的益处：来自伦敦地铁网络的有力证据》</a>，Larcom et al 2017</li><li data-pid=\"xM8jpkmV\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/economics/2016-michaels.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《重置城市网络：117--2012 AD》</a>，Michaels &amp; Rauch 2016；<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/economics/perpetuities/2021-heldring.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《修士、绅士与实业家：英国修道院解散的长期影响》</a>，Heldring et al 2021（参见有关<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/economics/perpetuities/index\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">永久存续安排</a>/<i><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/narrowing-circle#ancestors\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">waqfs</a></i> 会把错误固化下来的批评）</li><li data-pid=\"yFDz6gcN\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=3819317\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《Lehman 的「柠檬」：职业中断会影响顶尖的 5% 人群吗？》</a>，Fedyk &amp; Hodson 2021</li><li data-pid=\"vlJUZx9H\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/economics/2021-arellanobover.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《流离失所、多样性与流动性：日裔美国人拘禁的职业影响》</a>，Arellano-Bover 2021</li><li data-pid=\"9HXl8RK6\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/economics/automation/2024-barros.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《自然灾害与金融科技的采用》</a>，Barros et al 2024</li><li data-pid=\"51cVr-5O\">火灾（<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://academic.oup.com/past/article/265/1/97/7625037\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">背景</a>）：</li><ul><li data-pid=\"tP7SGWTA\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.248.7497&amp;rep=rep1&amp;type=pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《夷平旧金山：将 1906 年灾难作为城市再开发的自然实验》</a>，Siodla 2012；<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/economics/georgism/2021-pennington.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《新建住房会导致人口迁离吗？——旧金山住房建设的供给与需求效应》</a>，Pennington 2021</li><li data-pid=\"0zJ2t4aW\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/economics/2017-hornbeck.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《创造性破坏：城市增长的障碍与 1872 年波士顿大火》</a>，Hornbeck &amp; Keniston 2017（可与<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Limits-Power-Process-Christine-1986-04-30/dp/B01F9GNNFI/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《权力的限度：大火与美国城市增长进程》</a>（Rosen 1986）相比较）</li><li data-pid=\"CO8XE88R\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://eprints.lse.ac.uk/88694/1/dp1542.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《十亿英镑的损失：伦敦大轰炸与集聚经济学》</a>，Dericks &amp; Koster 2018（与 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/economics/2020-lin-2.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Lin 2020</a> 形成对照）</li><li data-pid=\"sHJZbnS1\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/economics/georgism/2022-liao.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《野火对加利福尼亚市政当局的财政影响》</a>，Liao &amp; Kousky 2022</li></ul></ul><li data-pid=\"OIyJy-sr\"><b>决策</b>：</li><ul><li data-pid=\"38--aO2w\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://docs.iza.org/dp11308.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《做出重大决定：迁居对美国陆军人员婚姻的影响》</a>，Carter &amp; Wozniak 2018</li><li data-pid=\"eEkL_s24\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"http://www.econweb.umd.edu/~pope/westpointtiming.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《时机决定一切：来自大学专业选择的证据》</a>，Patterson et al 2019</li><li data-pid=\"CcPCk1aA\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/psychology/cognitive-bias/2020-levitt.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《正面还是反面：抛硬币对重大人生决定及后续幸福感的影响》</a>，Levitt 2020</li><li data-pid=\"05mWsygu\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://doughanley.com/files/papers/thompson_hanley_wikipedia.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《科学由 Wikipedia 塑造：来自随机对照试验的证据》</a>，Thompson et al 2017；<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.marit.hinnosaar.net/wikipediamatters.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《Wikipedia 很重要》</a>，Hinnosaar et al 2019</li><li data-pid=\"1VjkEuG2\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/economics/2022-nakamura.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《搬迁的馈赠：流动性冲击的代际后果》</a>，Nakamura et al 2022</li></ul><li data-pid=\"rp6TC6DQ\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/creative_destruction\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">创造性破坏</a>；「<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porter_hypothesis\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">波特假说</a>」；<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/equity_premium_puzzle\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">股权溢价之谜</a></li><li data-pid=\"qBjZVeHF\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.law.nyu.edu/sites/default/files/upload_documents/Property Monopoly.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《财产是垄断的别称：以频谱、公司与土地的部分共同所有权促进高效议价》</a>，Posner &amp; Weyl 2016</li><li data-pid=\"lNbIkA87\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/492058.full\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《现实环境中的探索》</a>，Schulz et al 2018（这篇论文颇有意思，但并未明确证实存在次优探索；它使用了一个极其庞大的数据集，其中收录了个人通过 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deliveroo\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Deliveroo</a> 下达的餐厅订单）</li><li data-pid=\"HoTjJqQJ\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.03526\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《人类流动中存在守恒量的证据》</a>，Alessandretti et al 2016（人们只会造访少数实体地点；尽管他们确实会不断探索新地点 &amp; 变换活动地点，但似乎也存在一个类似<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunbar’s_number\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">邓巴数</a>的对应量，这提示，人类轻松规划/记住经常涉及超过 ~25 个地点的活动的能力可能存在局限）</li><li data-pid=\"47GHVtGo\">一个颇有意思的虚构例子或许是《小马宝莉》中的一集<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://mlp.fandom.com/wiki/Applejack's_&quot;Day&quot;_Off\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《Applejack 的「休息日」》</a>。</li><li data-pid=\"RdQFFH2Q\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.npr.org/sections/alltechconsidered/2017/06/08/531796329/eager-to-burst-his-own-bubble-a-techie-made-apps-to-randomize-his-life\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《急于戳破自己的泡沫，一名科技从业者开发应用，让自己的生活随机起来》</a></li><li data-pid=\"MS4Yoxnk\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/psychology/neuroscience/2021-camerer.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《神经自动驾驶与习惯的情境敏感性》</a>，Camerer &amp; Li 2021</li><li data-pid=\"etO9lq7P\"><b>另见</b>：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/backstop\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《进化是强化学习的后盾》</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>，<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/sunk-cost\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《沉没成本》</a>，<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://gwern.net/socks\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《论袜子多少才算够》</a></li></ul><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 演化：强化学习的最终保障 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1944108824375060346\" href=\"#/post/1944108824375060346\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"2062834806409401236","title":"让外包真正派上用场很难","author":"Gwern Branwen","votes":19,"minutes":13,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · Gwern Branwen"},{"id":"2063667653055603557","title":"人工智能需要好奇心吗？","author":"Nate Soares","votes":50,"minutes":7,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · Gwern Branwen"},{"id":"1944108824375060346","title":"演化：强化学习的最终保障","author":"Gwern Branwen","votes":12,"minutes":70,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"24025028685","title":"平庸的无能","author":"Gwern Branwen","votes":122,"minutes":5,"reason":"延伸引用本文"},{"id":"20351832676","title":"非常规小团体的惊人效能","author":"Gwern Branwen","votes":83,"minutes":8,"reason":"延伸引用本文"}],"rec_bridge":[{"id":"1972234251777840886","title":"创造力、乐趣与内在动机的形式化理论","author":"Jürgen Schmidhuber","votes":30,"minutes":22,"reason":"跨学派视角 · Jürgen Schmidhuber"},{"id":"2064048381673084062","title":"提升生产力与执行速度的一些理由","author":"Dan Luu","votes":39,"minutes":22,"reason":"跨学派视角 · Dan Luu"},{"id":"2040752225060902476","title":"寻找上行风险","author":"Neel Nanda","votes":152,"minutes":12,"reason":"跨学派视角 · Neel Nanda"},{"id":"24426750334","title":"「再努力点」在某些情况下可能是个糟糕的策略","author":"Sasha Chapin","votes":65,"minutes":2,"reason":"跨学派视角 · Sasha Chapin"},{"id":"1979480219023869096","title":"想入场？你起码得读过一本书。","author":"Ludicity","votes":262,"minutes":16,"reason":"跨学派视角 · Ludicity"}],"rec_answers":[]}